@startuml remote-workplace-attach
!theme plain
' Source: relux-works/curator-spec PR #134 (CIP-0009 revision 2, commit 5100b46), cips/diagrams; adapted. Updated 2026-10-12 for the accepted review findings F-7 (durable effect claims) and F-19 (service principal, stub as login shell, executions).
title Remote workplace (v1.3, after Curator CIP-0009 and review findings F-7, F-19): a remote worker turn: the harness has no local tools; the relay (harness identity) forwards to the bridge service (bridge identity), which carries every tool call and the mailbox over ONE SSH connection from the donor to our host; our host never connects back

box "Donor machine: harness identity (sandboxed, egress = proxy only)" #WhiteSmoke
  participant "Harness\n(Claude / Codex / Muse, lockdown plan)" as H
  participant "swarma-remote-tools\n(stdio relay; no keys, no network)" as MCP
  participant "Provider proxy" as PX
end box
box "Donor machine: bridge identity (keys, audit, cursors)" #WhiteSmoke
  participant "Bridge service\n(supervisor + SSH client + signer + admission)" as SUP
end box
box "Our host" #WhiteSmoke
  participant "sshd + root-owned stub\n(login shell of the workplace user;\nrelays the channel only)" as STUB
  participant "Workplace service\n(service principal: policy, caps,\neffect claims, audit, cert renewal)" as RB
  participant "Workplace\n(OS-user account class, swarma-workplace-exec/1;\negress always enforced)" as WP
  participant "Bridge\n(broker, mailbox, M3)" as BR
end box
participant "Orchestrator" as O

== standing connection ==
SUP -> STUB: ssh workplace-user@host with K_ssh (short user-CA certificate); host key checked against the pin on EVERY connection (no TOFU)
STUB -> RB: relay the channel to the service's Unix socket (peer UID + active generation checked)
RB --> SUP: hello {versions:[1]} / swarma-rb/1 channel open (bounded CBOR frames, flow credits)
SUP -> RB: policy.get
RB --> SUP: workplace policy {tools, write scope, network, limits, env_allow} -> effective tool set
note right of STUB: Match block: root-owned AuthorizedKeysFile, restrict, no forwarding, no PTY,\nno user rc/env; forced command by absolute path. The stub IS the login shell:\nsshd runs forced commands via the login shell, so no ~/.zshenv or ~/.bashrc is ever read.\nNothing that enforces policy runs as the workplace user. Reconnect is the donor side's job.

== launch ==
SUP -> SUP: obtain the composed plan from the construction site (agents-management);\ncheck expect_pin, tool_posture=lockdown, permissions=remote-auto, policy generation, qualified tuple;\nvalidate the expanded launch against the generated policy; resolve credential_binding/1
SUP -> H: start as the harness identity under the Seatbelt profile\n(e.g. claude --restricted --tools "" --strict-mcp-config --mcp-config <protected> --settings <protected>\n--setting-sources "" --disable-slash-commands --permission-prompts none --allowedTools mcp__swarma-remote-tools__*;\ntoken in the harness environment only, CIP-0010)
H -> MCP: MCP initialize; tools/list = effective set (policy intersection)

== task arrives ==
O -> BR: signed task message to the worker (snapshot of one element)
BR -> BR: verify signature, grant, decision guard, fence; mailbox record; cursor++
BR -> RB: mailbox.notify {message_id, cursor} (advisory)
RB -> SUP: frame mailbox.notify
SUP -> RB: mailbox.read {from_cursor}
RB -> BR: read
BR --> RB: items + verification records
RB --> SUP: frames
SUP -> SUP: DONOR-SIDE ADMISSION: verification record present, target binding = this worker,\nunexpired, not fenced/revoked, delivery mode allowed; dedup by message_id; persist; cursor++
SUP -> H: next turn through the session-input adapter: "validated message <id>" + snapshot
SUP -> RB: mailbox.applied {message_id} (application receipt, distinct from the transport reply)

== work ==
loop each tool call
  H -> MCP: tools/call bash {cmd, cwd, timeout}
  MCP -> SUP: forward over the relay socket (peer credentials checked)
  SUP -> SUP: audit line {tool, args_sha256, bytes, at}; budget counters (trusted side)
  SUP -> RB: frame exec {id, op_key, cmd, cwd, env (env_allow only), timeout_s <= policy, max_output_bytes <= policy, lease_s}
  RB -> RB: durable effect claim {binding generation, op_key, canonical-args digest} BEFORE the effect;\nfreshness window checked; mismatching reuse refuses
  RB -> WP: start as a launcher execution under the workplace user (start receipt, lease);\naudit {who, what, when, policy id} stays with the service
  WP --> RB: stdout/stderr frames (seq), exit
  RB --> SUP: frames (result cached 10 min; the claim outlives the cache)
  SUP --> MCP: result
  MCP --> H: tool result
end
H -> PX: model API calls (the only egress of the harness identity)
alt the model requests a built-in tool (Bash, Edit, WebFetch ...)
  H -> H: harness returns an error tool result (tool not available);\nthe tripwire logs the name after dispatch and may end the turn
end
alt SSH channel drops mid-turn
  SUP -> SUP: pause the turn loop; running turn continues to its deadline;\ntool calls fail with channel_down (retryable); result post queued durably with its op_key
  SUP -> RB: reconnect with backoff; host key rechecked; catch up from the durable cursor;\nreplay-safe: a known claim answers the cached result or unknown_result, never a second effect
end

== result ==
H -> MCP: tools/call mailbox_post {binding, text} (offered only when the policy grants it)
MCP -> SUP: forward
SUP -> SUP: build the FINAL envelope (canonical bytes; audience/thread from the task record);\nsign with K_sig (never leaves the bridge identity)
SUP -> RB: frame mailbox.post {op_key, envelope_bytes, signature}
RB -> BR: verify K_sig signature, grant, freshness; admit
BR -> O: carry the bytes UNCHANGED under the worker's carrier account (distinct authority, audited) -> outcome proposal
@enduml
